  "tail_ms": 600,
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "text": "9:20 PM. Ten men step ashore in Mumbai. In ten minutes, five attacks begin."
    },
    {
      "text": "They had sailed from Karachi for thirty-eight hours — undetected."
    },
    {
      "text": "CST. Leopold Café. The Taj. The Oberoi. Nariman House."
    },
    {
      "text": "And a control room six hundred kilometers away, watching the news and giving orders by phone."
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1 AM, a blast tore through the Taj's central dome."
    },
    {
      "text": "For three days, the city held its breath."
    },
    {
      "text": "Until, sixty hours later, the Taj was finally declared secure."
    },
    {
      "text": "Sixty Hours. The hour-by-hour story of 26/11 — now on The Sisodia Files."
    }
  ],
